-- title:
--   Special fibre of the twisted tower: Gᶜᵥ⊗ G^eᵥ≅𝔽ₚ⊗ Lᵥ
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, $\mathcal{O}$ is an algebra over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal $(p)$, and $\mathcal{O}$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Fix $r$ and a Honda system $H_1$ for the element $p$ on $\mathcal{O}^r$ (a Dieudonné datum $(F,V)$ together with a submodule $L$ satisfying the usual four conditions), a tower $G_v$ of finite commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras with bialgebra transition maps $s_v\colon G_{v+1}\to G_v$, and additive maps $\pi_v\colon\mathcal{O}^r\to D(G_v)$ into the Dieudonné modules. Let $\mathcal{S}$ be a system of split coordinates for these data — integers $d,h^c,h^e$, towers $G^c_v,G^e_v$ of Hopf $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras with transitions $s^c_v,s^e_v$, maps $q^c_v\colon G_v\to G^c_v$, $\pi^e_v\colon G_v\to G^e_v$, a section $\sigma_v$, a splitting $\Theta_v\colon G_v\to G^c_v\otimes G^e_v$, a formal group law $\Phi_0$ in $d$ variables over $\mathbb{Z}/p$ with presentations $\kappa_v\colon(\mathbb{Z}/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to G^c_v$, an $\mathcal{O}$-tower $E_v$ with transitions $s^t_v$ and maps $\theta^e_v\colon\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}E_v\to G^e_v$, elements $\hat c$, submodules $M^c,M^{et}$, a basis $\alpha$ of $H_1.L$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ and series $\bar a$ — and assume $\mathcal{S}$ is `Lawful`: $h^c+h^e=r$, each $G^c_v$ is local and each $G^e_v$ reduced, both are finite cocommutative of ranks $p^{vh^c}$, $p^{vh^e}$, the transitions are surjective with kernels the $p^v$-torsion ideals, $q^c_v,\pi^e_v$ are surjective with the prescribed kernels, $\Theta_v$ is bijective and equals $(q^c_v\otimes\pi^e_v)\circ\Delta$, all maps are compatible with the towers, $G^e_v$ is formally unramified, $\Phi_0$ is commutative, $\kappa_v$ is surjective with kernel generated by the $p^v$-series of $\Phi_0$ and is given by adic evaluation, together with the remaining normalisations and compatibilities (summarised here). Let $\Phi$ be a commutative formal group law in $d$ variables over $\mathcal{O}$ reducing mod $p$ to $\Phi_0$, and $c_2(v)\in(E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}E_v)^d$ with all entries in the ideal $(p)$. Finally let $L_v$ be commutative Hopf $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, finite and free over $\mathcal{O}$, with bialgebra transitions $t_v\colon L_{v+1}\to L_v$, bialgebra maps $\iota_v\colon E_v\to L_v$ and algebra maps $\Psi_v\colon\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to L_v$ such that $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}L_v=p^{v(h^c+h^e)}$, $t_v\circ\iota_{v+1}=\iota_v\circ s^t_v$, $t_v\circ\Psi_{v+1}=\Psi_v$, the counit of each $\Psi_v(X_i)$ vanishes, $\Psi_v$ of the $p^v$-series of $\Phi$ lies in $(p)$, the induced map $E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}\mathcal{O}[[X]]\to L_v$ is surjective, and the comultiplication is twisted by $c_2$: $\Delta(\Psi_v X_i)=\Phi_i\bigl(\Psi_v X\otimes 1,\;\Phi\bigl(1\otimes\Psi_v X,\;(\iota_v\otimes\iota_v)(c_2(v))\bigr)\bigr)$, evaluated adically at the ideal $(p)$ of $L_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}L_v$. Then there exist bialgebra maps $e_v\colon G^c_v\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}/p}G^e_v\to\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}L_v$ such that each $e_v$ is bijective, $e_v(\kappa_v(\bar F)\otimes 1)=1\otimes\Psi_v(F)$ for every $F\in\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ with $\bar F$ its reduction, $e_v(1\otimes\theta^e_v(1\otimes y))=1\otimes\iota_v(y)$ for $y\in E_v$, and $s^c_v\otimes s^e_v$ followed by $e_v$ equals $e_{v+1}$ followed by $\mathrm{id}\otimes t_v$.
--
--   This is the identification of the special fibre of the twisted tower $(L_v)$ with the given tower of finite Hopf algebras, in the form $\Gamma\otimes k\cong G$ of Fontaine's lifting theorem: modulo $p$ the cocycle $c_2$ vanishes, so $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}L_v$ becomes the untwisted tensor product of the connected part presented by $\Phi_0$ and the étale part. Composed with the splitting $\Theta_v$ it supplies the comparison map in the conclusion of the lifting theorem, and it is used by [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_pDivisibleTower_bijective_map_mem_fontaineHodge_of_splitCoordinates_of_cocycle`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_pDivisibleTower_bijective_map_mem_fontaineHodge_of_splitCoordinates_of_cocycle).
